_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:63dbfad5b6667a769010c9f0b9083dc98848e284b1e13a467ed39e986c4b5f07","file":"preprints/The-joint-scaling-limit-of-critical-Ashkin-Teller-currents-October-6-2026/build/sections/02-model.tex","line":355,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"57bf295c3745b776529392e4f4dbccd514aad50db97b9b672d6e344cb4361c7e","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-joint-scaling-limit-of-critical-Ashkin-Teller-currents-October-6-2026/build/sections/02-model.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:63dbfad5b6667a769010c9f0b9083dc98848e284b1e13a467ed39e986c4b5f07","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-joint-scaling-limit-of-critical-Ashkin-Teller-currents-October-6-2026/build/sections/02-model.tex#L355"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every fixed pair $J>0$, $U\\le J$ with $\\sinh(2J)=e^{-2U}$,\nevery bounded Jordan domain $D$, and every admissible polygonal\napproximation as defined in \\cref{sec:lattice-domains},\n\\[\n \\bigl(H_\\delta,\\cC_\\delta^{\\rm w},\\cC_\\delta^{\\rm f},\n                         C_{\\partial,\\delta}\\bigr)\n \\ \\xrightarrow[\\delta\\downarrow0]{\\mathrm{law}}\\\n \\left(\\frac{h}{\\pi\\sqrt g},\\cC^{\\rm w},\\cC^{\\rm f},\n                         \\TVS{a}{a}(h)\\right).\n\\]\nThe height converges in \\(H^s_{\\rm loc}(D)\\) for every \\(s<-1\\).\nEach cluster collection converges in the matching topology just\ndefined, and the distinguished component converges in Hausdorff\ntopology. The continuum collections are locally finite above every\npositive diameter. All convergences are joint, and the same GFF\ndetermines both continuum collections."}
